# Compute cost

Compute jobs that agents launch on machines other than their own (cloud VMs,
GPUs, clusters) share one cap: at most $10,000 a day in total, across all
agents (decision D8 in `docs/template-plan.md`). There is no per-job limit.
Each task states its compute budget in US dollars, in the "Compute budget"
section of its Linear issue; a task that states none has a budget of $0.

Before launching a job, estimate its cost as machines × hours × price per
machine-hour. Stop and ask a person, giving the estimate and how you got it,
if:

- the `compute-jobs` skill doesn't exist yet. Until it does, no provider
  budget control enforces the daily cap, so every job needs approval;
- the job would take the task's total compute spend, including failed and
  retried runs, over its budget; or
- you can't estimate the job's cost.

Never work around a provider budget limit, for example by switching account or
provider.
